    "review": "Do not adopt the discarded positive performance expectation as evidence of legacy overlay behavior. The upstream overlay-keyboard spec keeps zero-tick checks without a subscriber but deletes subscription, dispatch and the expected one ApplicationRef.tick call after a subscriber. Nine of ten complete callbacks are unchanged; that does not establish equivalent keyboard delivery or application notification semantics. The import reorder and lint exemption removal require no owned change. Preserve existing legacy overlay tests and public peer delegation. Actual subscribed keyboard delivery, teardown, zoneful/zoneless behavior and advertised peer floors remain execution obligations."
  },
  "decision": "Do not adopt the discarded positive performance expectation as evidence of legacy overlay behavior. The upstream overlay-keyboard spec keeps zero-tick checks without a subscriber but deletes subscription, dispatch and the expected one ApplicationRef.tick call after a subscriber. Nine of ten complete callbacks are unchanged; that does not establish equivalent keyboard delivery or application notification semantics. The import reorder and lint exemption removal require no owned change. Preserve existing legacy overlay tests and public peer delegation. Actual subscribed keyboard delivery, teardown, zoneful/zoneless behavior and advertised peer floors remain execution obligations. Exact compiler/Node/RxJS/peer floors, consumer/SSR/browser gates, private command-source reconciliation and independent audit remain separate. No publication.",
